        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3678?u=052bce4348ce233441ab066be54855729010c81f&v=4",
                "login": "megalithic",
                "resourcePath": "/megalithic",
                "url": "https://github.com/megalithic"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "NONE",
            "body": "@echasnovski: as a follow-up to this, is there a way to make vit/cit use nvim-treesitter-textobject's for tag changing/selection/operations instead of of the capture group way from the mini.ai plugin?\r\n\r\nthe reason being is, with elixir and heex templates you can define custom html tags that ultimately point to an elixir function, so `<div><.custom_tag custom_attr=\"foo\">hi from custom tag</.custom_tag>` would point to a function `def custom_tag(assigns), do: \"\"` for instance; the present defaults in mini.ai don't seem to work with text object operations on those custom attributes, but the defaults with nvim-treesitter-textobjects do.\r\n\r\nhere's the impl of the textobject query for the heex filetype: https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter-textobjects/blob/master/queries/heex/textobjects.scm",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/echasnovski/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski\">@echasnovski</a>: as a follow-up to this, is there a way to make vit/cit use nvim-treesitter-textobject's for tag changing/selection/operations instead of of the capture group way from the mini.ai plugin?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">the reason being is, with elixir and heex templates you can define custom html tags that ultimately point to an elixir function, so <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;div&gt;&lt;.custom_tag custom_attr=\"foo\"&gt;hi from custom tag&lt;/.custom_tag&gt;</code> would point to a function <code class=\"notranslate\">def custom_tag(assigns), do: \"\"</code> for instance; the present defaults in mini.ai don't seem to work with text object operations on those custom attributes, but the defaults with nvim-treesitter-textobjects do.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">here's the impl of the textobject query for the heex filetype: <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter-textobjects/blob/master/queries/heex/textobjects.scm\">https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter-textobjects/blob/master/queries/heex/textobjects.scm</a></p>",
            "bodyText": "@echasnovski: as a follow-up to this, is there a way to make vit/cit use nvim-treesitter-textobject's for tag changing/selection/operations instead of of the capture group way from the mini.ai plugin?\nthe reason being is, with elixir and heex templates you can define custom html tags that ultimately point to an elixir function, so <div><.custom_tag custom_attr=\"foo\">hi from custom tag</.custom_tag> would point to a function def custom_tag(assigns), do: \"\" for instance; the present defaults in mini.ai don't seem to work with text object operations on those custom attributes, but the defaults with nvim-treesitter-textobjects do.\nhere's the impl of the textobject query for the heex filetype: https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter-textobjects/blob/master/queries/heex/textobjects.scm",
