                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "Yes, it might be possible. Try following suggestions from [this comment](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/110#issuecomment-1212277863). In your case the code seems to be exactly the same with `@function.outer` and `@function.inner` for `a` and `i` tag textobjects.\r\n\r\nAnother solution might be to modify default tag textobject specification to allow punctuation in tag name. It would be something like this (use `[%p%w]` instead of `%w`):\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.ai').setup({\r\n  custom_textobjects = {\r\n    t = { '<([%p%w]-)%f[^<%p%w][^<>]->.-</%1>', '^<.->().*()</[^/]->$' },\r\n  }\r\n})\r\n```",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Yes, it might be possible. Try following suggestions from <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/110#issuecomment-1212277863\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/110/hovercard\">this comment</a>. In your case the code seems to be exactly the same with <code class=\"notranslate\">@function.outer</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">@function.inner</code> for <code class=\"notranslate\">a</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">i</code> tag textobjects.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Another solution might be to modify default tag textobject specification to allow punctuation in tag name. It would be something like this (use <code class=\"notranslate\">[%p%w]</code> instead of <code class=\"notranslate\">%w</code>):</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"require('mini.ai').setup({\n  custom_textobjects = {\n    t = { '&lt;([%p%w]-)%f[^&lt;%p%w][^&lt;&gt;]-&gt;.-&lt;/%1&gt;', '^&lt;.-&gt;().*()&lt;/[^/]-&gt;$' },\n  }\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>mini.ai<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">custom_textobjects</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">t</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;([%p%w]-)%f[^&lt;%p%w][^&lt;&gt;]-&gt;.-&lt;/%1&gt;<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>^&lt;.-&gt;().*()&lt;/[^/]-&gt;$<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>},\n  }\n})</pre></div>",
                    "bodyText": "Yes, it might be possible. Try following suggestions from this comment. In your case the code seems to be exactly the same with @function.outer and @function.inner for a and i tag textobjects.\nAnother solution might be to modify default tag textobject specification to allow punctuation in tag name. It would be something like this (use [%p%w] instead of %w):\nrequire('mini.ai').setup({\n  custom_textobjects = {\n    t = { '<([%p%w]-)%f[^<%p%w][^<>]->.-</%1>', '^<.->().*()</[^/]->$' },\n  }\n})",
